<title>FINLAND: YIT PROPOSES REDEMPTION CLAUSE.</title>
<headline>YIT PROPOSES REDEMPTION CLAUSE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish construction group YIT-Yhtyma Oy said in a statement on Monday its board proposed a redemption clause to be included in the company's bylaws.</p>
<p>&quot;According to a proposal by YIT-Yhtyma's board, a shareholder with more than a third and/or more than half of shares ... has to make an offer to redeem the rest of the outstanding shares,&quot; YIT said.</p>
<p>YIT called an extra shareholders meeting for November 4.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
</text>
